      "content": "While statistical correlations can be useful for general risk modeling, using demographic data like race to weigh individual threats is unwarranted and often leads to unjustifiable biases that undermine the very security data you aim to protect. AI security systems should rely exclusively on specific, observable behaviors such as loitering duration, evasion of authority, or damage assessment rather than protected characteristics. Incorporating bias into an algorithm creates dangerous false positives that erode public trust and disproportionately affect minority communities, ultimately reducing the accuracy and effectiveness of the system overall.",
